card.statement:
Assume $q_i\neq 1$ for all $1 \le i \le n$. The elements $z_1,\dots,z_n$ are algebraically independent in $R$. Moreover, the set

\[
\b=\left\{y_{1}^{j_{1}}x_{1}^{i_{1}}...y_{n}^{j_{n}}x_{n}^{i_{n}},\; (j_{1},i_{1},...,j_{n},i_{n}) \in \N^{2n}, \;
i_kj_k=0, \, \forall 1 \le k \le n\right\}
\]

is a basis of $A_n^{\bar{q},\Lambda}$ regarded as a left or as a right $R$-module. Further, $\b$ is a basis of $B_n^{\bar{q},\Lambda}$ both as a left and as a right $R^\circ$-module.
